The game is fine. The controls and gameplay are pretty solid. Piloting helicopters to bring democracy or spread comunism else where has never been so fun. However:
Pros:
- Nice maps;
- Objective driven;
- Nice graphics;
- Nice gameplay;
- Not many bugs (and it's still in development);
- The community has a reasonable amount of players. I'll always find matches;
Cons:
- The guns in this game sound and feel really fake;
- The main menu is confusing;
- The server browser is trash (I don't even know how they managed to come up with something like that);
- Heatseeker is compeltely overpowed;
Suggestions:
- Give points for players putting soldiers on the objective;
- Reduce heatseeker hit probability;
- What about auto-balance?
Bugs:
- Sometimes hits are not being registered (this happened while flying and shoting an enemy in really close range);
- In the main menu, if you change the language it doesn't save next time you open the game;
- The filter of the search page is not saved if you go in for a match. You have to select it every time you come back from a match;
I think the game is quite funny. Totally worth it.

